---
description: Keep Featurely records in sync when working on tracked features, bugs, or errors. Resolve one project via list_projects first. Never invent Featurely IDs or statuses — query MCP first.
alwaysApply: false
---

When this workspace uses Featurely (the user mentions Featurely, a feature/bug/error/task ID, roadmap, or changelog):

- Call `list_projects` first, then query **one** project (match by name). If several are granted and none was chosen, list them and stop. Never fan out the same fetch across every project. Never guess project IDs or status keys (`list_workflow_statuses` before writes).
- Read live data through the `featurely` MCP server before answering. Do not invent IDs, vote counts, statuses, or stack traces.
- Board bugs (`list_bugs`) are not the same as SDK error reports (`list_errors`).
- If the user asks you to work on or fix a Featurely item, close the loop: set in-progress/investigating immediately, post status notes, then mark done/resolved and publish changelog (features/bugs only). Details are in the `featurely` skill.
- Writes only for the item they named, and only if that project has write scopes. Never bulk-mutate. Never DELETE.
- `actorName` is `"Cursor"`. Never paste API keys into chat or source.
- SDK install/config uses `featurely-docs` MCP and the package skills, not guessed APIs.
